From dab0736cdb59a1f394029e654d3eb394200a2b52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:53:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/32] B70-QSA-02: QSA block top-k on XPU and one dispatch
 function per indexer kernel

cooperative_topk/persistent_topk are CUDA-only csrc ops. Off CUDA, _topk now
routes by B70_QSA_TOPK (auto|native|torch):
- native: torch.ops._C.top_k_per_row_decode from vllm-xpu-kernels (SYCL,
  registered for kXPU) with next_n=1 and the per-row visible count as seq_lens;
  same contract (rows shorter than topK get 0..len-1 then -1).
- torch: exact and deterministic. Sorts an int64 key (order-preserving float32
  bits << 32 | inverted column), so exact ties break toward the lower column.
  ReLU-summed scores tie at exactly 0.0 at the top-k boundary often (81 of 338
  rows in a random prefill case), where float top-k picks arbitrarily.
- auto (default): native when the op is registered, else torch.

Decode and prefill tile/warp/stage choices move into _decode_launch_config and
_prefill_launch_config (XPU entries are untuned copies of the GB300 ones), and
the warmup uses the same helper as the launch. The decode scorer gains an
optional MIN_DOT_N constexpr (default 1 = the original kernel):
B70_QSA_MIN_DOT_N=16 pads its tl.dot N (query rows x 4 heads, 4 at a plain
decode) into DPAS range for tuning. Intel Triton has no dot minimum; N < 16
falls back to FMA and stays correct.
